# Project Analysis & Incomplete Frontend Review

This document provides a thorough analysis of the **FreshTrack** project, detailing key architectural pain points, UX inconsistencies, and incomplete frontend implementations.

---

## 🔍 Incomplete Frontend Items & Visual Bugs

### 1. Missing Branding on Landing Page Navbar
* **File**: [Landing.jsx](file:///c:/Projects/FreshTrack-main/frontend/src/pages/Landing.jsx#L25-L27)
* **Issue**: The brand container inside the landing page navbar is entirely empty:
  ```html
  <div className="flex items-center gap-2"></div>
  ```
  Users landing on the page see a blank space on the top-left where the application logo and title ("FreshTrack") should be.

### 2. Inconsistent Branding ("The Conservatory" vs "FreshTrack")
* **Files**: 
  * [Sidebar.jsx](file:///c:/Projects/FreshTrack-main/frontend/src/components/Sidebar.jsx#L24-L32) (Displays "The Conservatory")
  * [Login.jsx](file:///c:/Projects/FreshTrack-main/frontend/src/pages/Login.jsx#L151) & [Signup.jsx](file:///c:/Projects/FreshTrack-main/frontend/src/pages/Signup.jsx#L185) (Buttons say "Enter The Conservatory")
  * [TopNavBar.jsx](file:///c:/Projects/FreshTrack-main/frontend/src/components/TopNavBar.jsx#L19) (Displays "FreshTrack")
* **Issue**: The app refers to itself interchangeably as "The Conservatory" and "FreshTrack", creating a disjointed user experience.

### 3. Missing Sidebar Navigation for Profile Page
* **File**: [Sidebar.jsx](file:///c:/Projects/FreshTrack-main/frontend/src/components/Sidebar.jsx#L15-L19)
* **Issue**: The sidebar includes links for `Home`, `Dashboard`, and `Recipes`, but completely omits the `Profile` page. The only way to access the profile page is by clicking the small user avatar in the top navigation bar, which is non-obvious and poor UX.

### 4. Broken "Quick Meals" Recipe Filter
* **File**: [Recipes.jsx](file:///c:/Projects/FreshTrack-main/frontend/src/pages/Recipes.jsx#L81-L82)
* **Issue**: The "Quick Meals" filter is coded to look for recipes with a duration under 10 minutes:
  ```javascript
  filtered = filtered.filter(r => parseInt(r.time) < 10);
  ```
  However, in the backend recipe bank ([api.py](file:///c:/Projects/FreshTrack-main/backend/api.py#L60-L82)), all recipes (e.g., *Tomato Rasam*, *Lemon Rice*, *Apple Halwa*) have prep times ranging from 15 to 40 minutes. Consequently, selecting this filter always returns 0 results and falls back to showing all recipes.

### 5. Dead Code: Unused Fallback Captures
* **File**: [Dashboard.jsx](file:///c:/Projects/FreshTrack-main/frontend/src/pages/Dashboard.jsx#L12-L18)
* **Issue**: The `FALLBACK_CAPTURES` array is defined at the top of the file but is never used anywhere in the component rendering logic.

